:Namespace UCITests
    ⎕IO ⎕ML←1

    setup←{#.DeepOrange.LookupTables.createLookupTables ⍬}

    ⍝ A move is (from to promotion), as produced by MoveGeneration.
    ⍝ UCI long algebraic notation names the from and to squares, plus a
    ⍝ lowercase piece letter for a promotion. Castling is written as the
    ⍝ king's two-square move. The promotion piece in a move carries its
    ⍝ colour, so converting from UCI needs the side to move.

    move←{
        ⍝ ⍵ ←→ 'from to', promotion as a FEN piece letter ('' for none)
        ⍝ ← ←→ move (from to promotion)
        (squares promotion)←⍵
        (#.Tests.Helpers.sqs squares),pieceCode promotion
    }

    pieceCode←{
        ⍝ Pieces names each piece by its FEN letter.
        ⍝ ⍵ ←→ FEN piece letter, or '' for none
        ⍝ ← ←→ piece code; 0 for none
        0=≢⍵:0
        #.DeepOrange.Pieces ⎕VGET ⍵
    }

    ⍝ Each case: side to move (0 white, 1 black), squares, promotion
    ⍝ letter, UCI string. Cases hold plain data so the suite can be
    ⍝ loaded before the namespaces under test.
    CASES←(
        ('quiet pawn push'(0 'e2 e4' '' 'e2e4'))
        ('quiet knight move'(1 'g8 f6' '' 'g8f6'))
        ('capture'(0 'e4 d5' '' 'e4d5'))
        ('en passant capture'(0 'e5 d6' '' 'e5d6'))
        ('white kingside castling'(0 'e1 g1' '' 'e1g1'))
        ('white queenside castling'(0 'e1 c1' '' 'e1c1'))
        ('black kingside castling'(1 'e8 g8' '' 'e8g8'))
        ('black queenside castling'(1 'e8 c8' '' 'e8c8'))
        ('white promotion to queen'(0 'e7 e8' 'Q' 'e7e8q'))
        ('white promotion to rook'(0 'e7 e8' 'R' 'e7e8r'))
        ('white promotion to bishop'(0 'e7 e8' 'B' 'e7e8b'))
        ('white promotion to knight'(0 'e7 e8' 'N' 'e7e8n'))
        ('black promotion to queen'(1 'd2 d1' 'q' 'd2d1q'))
        ('black promotion to knight'(1 'd2 d1' 'n' 'd2d1n'))
        ('promotion with capture'(0 'g7 h8' 'Q' 'g7h8q'))
        ('corner squares'(0 'a1 h8' '' 'a1h8'))
    )

    test_writes_a_move_in_uci_notation_cases←CASES
    test_writes_a_move_in_uci_notation←{
        (side squares promotion uci)←⍵
        uci #.Tests.Framework.Assert.eq #.DeepOrange.UCI.moveToUCI move squares promotion
    }

    test_reads_a_move_from_uci_notation_cases←CASES
    test_reads_a_move_from_uci_notation←{
        (side squares promotion uci)←⍵
        (move squares promotion)#.Tests.Framework.Assert.eq side #.DeepOrange.UCI.uciToMove uci
    }

    ⍝ Start position, for the case tables below. Case tables are built
    ⍝ when the suite is loaded, when Helpers may not exist yet.
    START←'rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/8/8/PPPPPPPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 1'

    ⍝ applyMoves

    ⍝ Each case: start FEN, moves, FEN of the expected position.
    test_applies_moves_to_a_position_cases←(
        ('no moves'(START(0⍴⊂'')START))
        ('single move as a plain string'(START'e2e4' 'rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq e3 0 1'))
        ('single move as a one-item vector'(START(,⊂'e2e4')'rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq e3 0 1'))
        ('moves in the order played'(START('e2e4' 'e7e5' 'g1f3')'rnbqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 1 2'))
        ('capture'('rnbqkbnr/ppp1pppp/8/3p4/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq d6 0 2' 'e4d5' 'rnbqkbnr/ppp1pppp/8/3P4/8/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 2'))
        ('en passant capture'('k7/8/8/3pP3/8/8/8/K7 w - d6 0 1' 'e5d6' 'k7/8/3P4/8/8/8/8/K7 b - - 0 1'))
        ('white kingside castling'('r3k2r/8/8/8/8/8/8/R3K2R w KQkq - 0 1' 'e1g1' 'r3k2r/8/8/8/8/8/8/R4RK1 b kq - 1 1'))
        ('black queenside castling'('r3k2r/8/8/8/8/8/8/R3K2R b KQkq - 0 1' 'e8c8' '2kr3r/8/8/8/8/8/8/R3K2R w KQ - 1 2'))
        ('white promotion'('k7/4P3/8/8/8/8/8/K7 w - - 0 1' 'e7e8n' 'k3N3/8/8/8/8/8/8/K7 b - - 0 1'))
        ('black promotion'('k7/8/8/8/8/8/3p4/K7 b - - 0 1' 'd2d1q' 'k7/8/8/8/8/8/8/K2q4 w - - 0 2'))
        ('promotions by both sides in one list'('8/3P4/8/8/k7/7K/3p4/8 w - - 0 1'('d7d8q' 'd2d1q')'3Q4/8/8/8/k7/7K/8/3q4 w - - 0 2'))
    )
    test_applies_moves_to_a_position←{
        (start moves expected)←⍵
        (#.DeepOrange.Board.initFromFEN expected)#.Tests.Framework.Assert.eq(#.DeepOrange.Board.initFromFEN start)#.DeepOrange.UCI.applyMoves moves
    }

    ⍝ handlePositionCmd

    words←{
        ⍝ Space-separated text to its words, as the command dispatcher
        ⍝ passes them.
        ' '(≠⊆⊢)⍵
    }

    ⍝ Each case: arguments of the position command, FEN of the expected
    ⍝ position.
    test_handles_position_arguments_cases←(
        ('start position'('startpos' START))
        ('start position with moves'('startpos moves e2e4 e7e5 g1f3' 'rnbqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 1 2'))
        ('start position with a single move'('startpos moves e2e4' 'rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq e3 0 1'))
        ('start position with an empty move list'('startpos moves' START))
        ('fen'('fen r3k2r/8/8/8/8/8/8/R3K2R b KQkq - 3 17' 'r3k2r/8/8/8/8/8/8/R3K2R b KQkq - 3 17'))
        ('fen with moves'('fen r3k2r/8/8/8/8/8/8/R3K2R w KQkq - 0 1 moves e1g1 e8c8' '2kr3r/8/8/8/8/8/8/R4RK1 w - - 2 2'))
        ('fen with a black promotion'('fen k7/8/8/8/8/8/3p4/K7 b - - 0 1 moves d2d1q' 'k7/8/8/8/8/8/8/K2q4 w - - 0 2'))
        ('fen without move counters'('fen k7/8/8/8/8/8/8/K7 w - - moves a1a2' 'k7/8/8/8/8/8/K7/8 b - - 1 1'))
    )
    test_handles_position_arguments←{
        (args expected)←⍵
        (#.DeepOrange.Board.initFromFEN expected)#.Tests.Framework.Assert.eq #.DeepOrange.UCI.handlePositionCmd words args
    }

    ⍝ handle

    ⍝ The engine state is created by newState and passed through handle,
    ⍝ which returns the next state and the reply lines for one input line.

    session←{
        ⍝ ⍺ ←→ lookup tables
        ⍝ ⍵ ←→ input line, or a vector of them in the order sent
        ⍝ ← ←→ state after the last line, replies to the last line
        ⊃step/(⌽,⊆⍵),⊂(#.DeepOrange.UCI.newState ⍺)⍬
    }

    step←{
        ⍝ ⍺ ←→ input line
        ⍝ ⍵ ←→ state, replies to the previous line
        ⍝ ← ←→ state, replies to this line
        (⊃⍵)#.DeepOrange.UCI.handle ⍺
    }

    replies←{
        ⍝ ⍺ ←→ lookup tables
        ⍝ ⍵ ←→ input line, or a vector of them
        ⍝ ← ←→ replies to the last line
        2⊃⍺ session ⍵
    }

    bestmove←{
        ⍝ ⍵ ←→ replies to go
        ⍝ ← ←→ move named by the bestmove reply, which comes last
        0=≢⍵:#.Tests.Framework.Assert.fail'expected a reply but got none'
        reply←⊃⌽⍵
        ~'bestmove '≡9↑reply:#.Tests.Framework.Assert.fail'expected bestmove but got ',reply
        9↓reply
    }

    infoField←{
        ⍝ ⍺ ←→ field name, e.g. 'nodes'
        ⍝ ⍵ ←→ info line
        ⍝ ← ←→ word following the field name; '' when there is none
        fields←words ⍵
        (1+fields⍳⊂⍺)⊃fields,2⍴⊂''
    }

    isLegal←{
        ⍝ ⍺ ←→ lookup tables
        ⍝ ⍵ ←→ FEN, UCI move
        (fen uci)←⍵
        position←#.DeepOrange.Board.initFromFEN fen
        side←(2⊃position)[#.DeepOrange.GameState.side]
        (⊂side #.DeepOrange.UCI.uciToMove uci)∊↓⍺ #.DeepOrange.MoveGeneration.generateLegalMoves position
    }

    ⍝ A position where the side to move has exactly one legal move, a8a7.
    ONE_MOVE←'k7/8/8/8/8/8/8/1R5K b - - 0 1'

    test_uci_identifies_the_engine_by_name←{
        #.Tests.Framework.Assert.ok'id name '≡8↑⊃⍺ replies'uci'
    }

    test_uci_identifies_the_author←{
        #.Tests.Framework.Assert.ok'id author '≡10↑2⊃⍺ replies'uci'
    }

    test_uci_ends_with_uciok←{
        'uciok'#.Tests.Framework.Assert.eq⊃⌽⍺ replies'uci'
    }

    test_isready_replies_readyok←{
        (,⊂'readyok')#.Tests.Framework.Assert.eq ⍺ replies'isready'
    }

    test_go_replies_with_a_legal_move_from_the_start_position←{
        #.Tests.Framework.Assert.ok ⍺ isLegal #.Tests.Helpers.START(bestmove ⍺ replies'go')
    }

    test_go_ignores_search_parameters←{
        #.Tests.Framework.Assert.ok ⍺ isLegal #.Tests.Helpers.START(bestmove ⍺ replies'go wtime 60000 btime 60000 winc 0 binc 0')
    }

    test_position_has_no_reply←{
        0 #.Tests.Framework.Assert.eq≢⍺ replies'position startpos moves e2e4'
    }

    test_go_plays_from_a_position_given_by_fen←{
        'a8a7'#.Tests.Framework.Assert.eq bestmove ⍺ replies('position fen ',ONE_MOVE)'go'
    }

    test_go_plays_from_a_position_after_its_moves←{
        ⍝ After b2b1 the black king on a8 has only a7.
        lines←'position fen k7/8/8/8/8/8/1R6/7K w - - 0 1 moves b2b1' 'go'
        'a8a7'#.Tests.Framework.Assert.eq bestmove ⍺ replies lines
    }

    test_go_reports_the_search_in_an_info_line_before_the_bestmove←{
        r←⍺ replies'go'
        (2 'info ')#.Tests.Framework.Assert.eq(≢r)(5↑⊃r)
    }

    test_go_reports_the_search_depth←{
        (,'4')#.Tests.Framework.Assert.eq'depth'infoField⊃⍺ replies'go'
    }

    test_go_reports_the_positions_searched←{
        ⍝ Depth four from the start position: the root and its 20 children
        ⍝ are always searched, and pruning skips part of the full tree of
        ⍝ 1+20+400+8902+197281 positions.
        nodes←⊃2⊃⎕VFI'nodes'infoField⊃⍺ replies'go'
        #.Tests.Framework.Assert.ok(21<nodes)∧nodes<206604
    }

    test_go_reports_the_best_move_as_the_principal_variation←{
        r←⍺ replies'go'
        (bestmove r)#.Tests.Framework.Assert.eq'pv'infoField⊃r
    }

    test_go_sends_only_the_null_move_when_there_is_no_legal_move←{
        lines←'position fen k7/1Q6/1K6/8/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1' 'go'
        (,⊂'bestmove 0000')#.Tests.Framework.Assert.eq ⍺ replies lines
    }

    test_go_replies_with_the_null_move_when_checkmated←{
        lines←'position fen k7/1Q6/1K6/8/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1' 'go'
        '0000'#.Tests.Framework.Assert.eq bestmove ⍺ replies lines
    }

    test_ucinewgame_resets_to_the_start_position←{
        lines←('position fen ',ONE_MOVE)'ucinewgame' 'go'
        #.Tests.Framework.Assert.ok ⍺ isLegal #.Tests.Helpers.START(bestmove ⍺ replies lines)
    }

    test_ucinewgame_has_no_reply←{
        0 #.Tests.Framework.Assert.eq≢⍺ replies'ucinewgame'
    }

    test_ignores_extra_whitespace_between_tokens←{
        lines←('  position   fen  ',ONE_MOVE,'  ')'  go  '
        'a8a7'#.Tests.Framework.Assert.eq bestmove ⍺ replies lines
    }

    test_ignores_an_unknown_command←{
        lines←('position fen ',ONE_MOVE)'xyzzy 42' 'go'
        'a8a7'#.Tests.Framework.Assert.eq bestmove ⍺ replies lines
    }

    test_unknown_command_has_no_reply←{
        0 #.Tests.Framework.Assert.eq≢⍺ replies'xyzzy 42'
    }

    test_ignores_an_empty_line←{
        0 #.Tests.Framework.Assert.eq≢⍺ replies''
    }

    test_new_state_is_not_finished←{
        0 #.Tests.Framework.Assert.eq #.DeepOrange.UCI.finished #.DeepOrange.UCI.newState ⍺
    }

    test_quit_finishes_the_session←{
        1 #.Tests.Framework.Assert.eq #.DeepOrange.UCI.finished⊃⍺ session'quit'
    }

    test_other_commands_do_not_finish_the_session←{
        0 #.Tests.Framework.Assert.eq #.DeepOrange.UCI.finished⊃⍺ session'isready'
    }

    ⍝ infoLine

    ⍝ Each case: depth, score in centipawns, nodes, time in milliseconds,
    ⍝ best move, expected info line. Nodes per second are truncated to an
    ⍝ integer; a search under a millisecond counts as one millisecond.
    test_formats_an_info_line_cases←(
        ('centipawn score'((2 100 421 15(13 29 0))'info depth 2 score cp 100 nodes 421 time 15 nps 28066 pv e2e4'))
        ('negative score with a minus sign'((3 ¯50 1000 200(13 29 0))'info depth 3 score cp -50 nodes 1000 time 200 nps 5000 pv e2e4'))
        ('zero score'((1 0 21 4(13 29 0))'info depth 1 score cp 0 nodes 21 time 4 nps 5250 pv e2e4'))
        ('search under a millisecond'((1 0 21 0(13 29 0))'info depth 1 score cp 0 nodes 21 time 0 nps 21000 pv e2e4'))
        ('promotion in the principal variation'((1 800 5 1(53 61 5))'info depth 1 score cp 800 nodes 5 time 1 nps 5000 pv e7e8q'))
    )
    test_formats_an_info_line←{
        (search expected)←⍵
        expected #.Tests.Framework.Assert.eq #.DeepOrange.UCI.infoLine search
    }

    ⍝ UCI reports a mate as the number of moves to it, not half-moves,
    ⍝ negative when the side to move is the one being mated.

    mateScore←{
        ⍝ ⍵ ←→ score
        ⍝ ← ←→ score field of the info line for a depth-3 search
        info←#.DeepOrange.UCI.infoLine 3 ⍵ 100 10(13 29 0)
        ('score'infoField info),' ',('mate'infoField info),'cp'infoField info
    }

    test_reports_mate_in_one_for_the_side_to_move←{
        'mate 1'#.Tests.Framework.Assert.eq mateScore #.DeepOrange.Search.MATE-1
    }

    test_reports_mate_in_two_for_the_side_to_move←{
        'mate 2'#.Tests.Framework.Assert.eq mateScore #.DeepOrange.Search.MATE-3
    }

    test_reports_being_mated_in_one_as_negative←{
        'mate -1'#.Tests.Framework.Assert.eq mateScore 2-#.DeepOrange.Search.MATE
    }

    test_reports_being_mated_in_two_as_negative←{
        'mate -2'#.Tests.Framework.Assert.eq mateScore 4-#.DeepOrange.Search.MATE
    }

:EndNamespace
